## Section 1 — Mutual Fund Domain (Your Strongest Domain)

### What You Already Know
- MF Central (MFC): the centralized MF transaction platform built by CAMS + KFintech
- RTA bulk upload: BSE Star MF / NSE NMF II / MF Utilities bulk transaction files (CSV/XML formats)
- MF onboarding: KYC via KRA (CKYC, CAMS KRA, KFintech KRA), FATCA/CRS, nominee registration, bank mandate (NACH/eNACH)
- Transaction types: SIP, lump sum, switch, STP, SWP, redemption, IDCW payout

### Problem Areas Where AI Adds Real Value

#### Idea 1A — KYC Document Intelligence Engine
**The Problem:**
MF distributors (MFDs) and RIAs receive scanned KYC documents daily — Aadhaar, PAN, passport, bank statements. Manual verification is slow, error-prone, and a compliance bottleneck.

**The AI Layer (PerceptionX-style):**
- Replace YOLO with document OCR + classification models
- Your existing pipeline: Video upload → GPU → detection → MongoDB becomes: Document upload → GPU OCR → field extraction → MongoDB
- Models needed: Document classification (PAN vs Aadhaar vs bank statement), field OCR, signature detection, photo extraction

**What the Product Does:**
```
MFD uploads scanned KYC packet (PDF or image)
  → AI extracts: PAN number, DOB, address, photo, signature
  → Cross-checks against CKYC/KRA API
  → Flags: mismatches, expired documents, illegible fields
  → Returns structured JSON ready for RTA upload
  → 90% reduction in manual data entry time
```

**Revenue Model:** SaaS per-document pricing (₹2–5/document). Target: 500 MFDs → ₹50L+/month at scale.

**Technical Fit with Your Stack:**
- Node.js → Python FastAPI → GPU inference: identical architecture
- Modal GPU for OCR inference: same pattern
- MongoDB: store extracted fields per document
- New: integrate CKYC/KRA REST APIs for validation

---

#### Idea 1B — RTA Bulk Upload Error Predictor
**The Problem:**
RTA bulk upload files (for BSE Star MF, NSE NMF II, MFU) have strict format requirements. A single row error rejects the entire batch. Distributors lose hours re-formatting files.

**The AI Layer:**
Not vision-based — this is an ML classification + rule engine:
- Trained on historical upload errors (your own or crowd-sourced)
- Predicts which rows will fail before upload
- Auto-corrects common issues (date format, folio number format, ISIN mapping)

**What the Product Does:**
```
Distributor uploads their transaction CSV
  → AI validates every row in <5 seconds
  → Highlights errors with suggested fixes
  → One-click auto-correct for known patterns
  → Preview of clean file before RTA submission
```

**Technical Fit:**
- No GPU needed (CSV processing is pure Python pandas + sklearn)
- React frontend with drag-drop CSV upload: already built in PerceptionX
- This is the simplest to build of all ideas here

**Revenue Model:** ₹999–₹2999/month SaaS for MFDs. High retention because used daily.

---

#### Idea 1C — MF Onboarding Video KYC Analyzer
**The Problem:**
SEBI mandates Video KYC (V-KYC) for certain investor categories. Current V-KYC platforms are expensive and provide no analytics to MFDs.

**The AI Layer (Direct PerceptionX extension):**
- Your video inference pipeline is DIRECTLY applicable here
- Replace YOLO traffic detection with: face liveness detection, document frame extraction, audio transcription
- ByteTrack → face tracking across the V-KYC session

**What the Product Does:**
```
Investor does video call with MFD agent
  → AI analyzes: face liveness (blink, head turn), document visibility, lighting quality
  → Extracts key frames (PAN shown to camera, face clearly visible)
  → Flags: poor lighting, document not readable, face not centered
  → Compliance report: "V-KYC session score: 87/100, 2 issues flagged"
  → Auto-archives KYC frames to Cloudinary (already built)
```

**Technical Fit:** Nearly identical to PerceptionX — your stack literally does 80% of this already.

**Revenue Model:** ₹50–200 per V-KYC session. MFDs doing 100+ onboardings/month → high LTV.

---

## Section 2 — Banking Sector

### Problem Areas

#### Idea 2A — Bank Branch Queue Intelligence (Vision AI)
**The Problem:**
Bank branches have poor queue management. Customers wait without visibility. Branch managers have no data on peak hours, average wait times, or teller efficiency.

**The AI Layer (Your Exact PerceptionX Stack):**
- CCTV camera feed → Your video pipeline
- YOLO detects: people in queue, teller windows occupied/free, counter positions
- ByteTrack: tracks individual customers through the queue journey
- Analytics: avg wait time, peak hours, teller utilization %

**What the Product Does:**
```
CCTV feed (IP camera or recorded video) → PerceptionX pipeline
  → Detects: queue length, active tellers, waiting area density
  → Analytics dashboard: real-time queue depth, historical trends
  → Alerts: "Queue > 15 people at Counter 3 — open backup counter"
  → Compliance: "Priority banking customers not being served faster"
  → Report to branch manager + regional manager
```

**Technical Fit:** This IS PerceptionX. Your traffic monitoring vertical is literally a queue counter. Replace "car/truck" classes with "person/teller_window/counter".

**Revenue Model:** ₹15,000–₹50,000/branch/month SaaS. Even 10 branches = ₹5L+/month.

---

#### Idea 2B — Cheque & Document Fraud Detection
**The Problem:**
Banks process millions of cheques. Manual fraud detection is slow. Altered cheques (amount manipulation, signature forgery) cause significant losses.

**The AI Layer:**
- Vision model trained on cheque images: detect tampering, erasure marks, ink inconsistencies
- Signature verification: compare against registered signature specimen
- MICR line validation

**Technical Fit:** Moderate. Requires new training data (cheque dataset). Your inference pipeline fits perfectly.

---

#### Idea 2C — ATM Surveillance Analytics
**The Problem:**
Banks need to detect: ATM skimming device attachment, card trapping, shoulder surfing, vandalism. Current solutions are expensive and from foreign vendors.

**The AI Layer (Perfect PerceptionX Fit):**
- ATM CCTV feed → Your video pipeline
- YOLO: detects foreign objects on card slot, suspicious behaviors, loitering
- ByteTrack: tracks individuals near ATM
- Alerts: "Person standing < 0.5m from another person at ATM for >30 seconds"

**Technical Fit:** HIGH. Your pipeline handles exactly this use case. Fine-tune best11.pt on ATM-specific classes.

---

## Section 3 — Stock Market & Liquidity Domain

### Problem Areas

#### Idea 3A — Trading Floor / Dealer Room Activity Monitor
**The Problem:**
Investment banks and broking houses need surveillance of dealer rooms — SEBI compliance requires monitoring for unauthorized communication, unusual behavior during sensitive periods (merger announcements, IPO lock-up periods).

**The AI Layer:**
- Dealer room CCTV → your video pipeline
- Detect: mobile phone usage (prohibited), unauthorized personnel, unusual gatherings
- Time-stamp behavioral events for compliance log

**Technical Fit:** HIGH. Adapts directly from PerceptionX traffic monitoring.

---

#### Idea 3B — Stock Market News Sentiment + Liquidity Predictor
**The Problem:**
Retail traders and small fund managers lack real-time tools to correlate news sentiment with stock liquidity (bid-ask spread, order book depth).

**The AI Layer (Text AI, not Vision):**
- NLP model: news sentiment analysis (positive/negative/neutral per stock/sector)
- ML model: predict liquidity compression events (wide spreads) based on sentiment + time of day + sector
- Output: "HDFC Bank — news sentiment turning negative, liquidity risk: HIGH for next 2 hours"

**Technical Fit:** Moderate. Different AI stack (NLP vs vision) but same Node + Python + React + MongoDB architecture.

---

#### Idea 3C — IPO Subscription Analytics Dashboard
**The Problem:**
During IPO subscription windows, retail investors and HNIs want real-time analytics on subscription status, GMP (grey market premium) trends, and category-wise data.

**The AI Layer:**
- Web scraping + ML: predict final subscription multiples from hourly data
- No vision needed — pure data analytics

**Technical Fit:** Easy to build, but highly competitive (many free tools exist). LOW differentiation.

---

## Section 4 — Insurance Sector (Adjacent to MF/Banking)

#### Idea 4A — Motor Insurance Claim Video Analyzer
**The Problem:**
Motor insurance claims require photo/video evidence of vehicle damage. Manual assessment is slow, inconsistent, and prone to fraud.

**The AI Layer (Your Exact Stack):**
- Policyholder uploads damage video → Your PerceptionX pipeline
- YOLO (fine-tuned): detects damage zones on vehicle (front bumper, door dent, windshield crack)
- Classifies damage severity: minor / moderate / major
- Generates structured damage report for surveyor

**What the Product Does:**
```
Customer uploads 30-second video of damaged vehicle
  → AI detects: damage type, location on vehicle, severity
  → Outputs: "Front bumper: Major damage, Left door: Minor scratch"
  → Pre-fills claim form with detected damage
  → Flags: inconsistencies between damage and claimed accident type
  → Estimated repair cost range
```

**Technical Fit:** EXTREMELY HIGH. This is almost identical to PerceptionX. Just retrain best11.pt on vehicle damage dataset.

**Revenue Model:** ₹50–150 per claim assessed. Target: 5–10 insurers → massive volume.

**Market Opportunity:** India processes ~50 lakh motor insurance claims/year. Even 1% market share = 50,000 claims/month.

---

#### Idea 4B — Life Insurance KYC + Medical Document Analyzer
**Similar to Idea 1A** but for insurance: extract data from medical reports, lab tests, hospital discharge summaries for underwriting.

---

## Section 5 — Emerging / High-Potential Hybrid Ideas

#### Idea 5A — MF Branch / Distributor Office Intelligence
Combine Vision AI + MF domain:
- MFD office CCTV → detect client footfall, meeting duration, peak hours
- Correlate with AUM data: "branches with longest client meetings have 2.3× higher SIP conversion"
- Analytics for AMC distribution teams

#### Idea 5B — Compliance Monitoring for SEBI-Regulated Entities
SEBI requires investment advisers (RIAs) to record and store client meeting recordings. AI analyzes:
- Was risk profiling discussion complete? (keyword detection in audio)
- Was product suitability explained? (compliance checklist from transcript)
- Flags non-compliant advisory sessions

