## Section 8 — Technical Architecture Mapping

### How PerceptionX Stack Becomes Your Fintech Product

```
PerceptionX Component          →    Fintech Product Component
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
React SPA (Home, Analytics)    →    MFD Portal / Bank Dashboard
Video upload (drag-drop)       →    Document / Video upload
Node.js Express API            →    Same — orchestration layer
Python FastAPI                 →    Same — inference engine
YOLO best11.pt                 →    best_vkyc.pt / best_damage.pt
ByteTrack (object tracking)    →    Face tracking across V-KYC session
MongoDB files collection       →    Same — per-session metadata
MongoDB analytics collection   →    Compliance reports, session scores
Cloudinary (raw video)         →    V-KYC session recording storage
Cloudinary (processed video)   →    Annotated compliance review video
Modal GPU (T4)                 →    Same — inference workload
isProcessed polling            →    Same — session analysis complete flag
Socket.io (live detect)        →    Live V-KYC session monitoring
recharts dashboard             →    Compliance analytics dashboard
```

**New components you'll need to add:**

```
+ KYC API Layer
  → CKYC REST API (Central KYC Registry)
  → KRA API: CAMS KRA, KFintech KRA, NDML KRA
  → PAN verification: Income Tax PAN verify API
  → Bank account validation: Penny drop API (Razorpay / Cashfree)

+ Regulatory Layer
  → Session audit log (immutable, timestamped)
  → Consent management (DPDP Act 2023 compliance)
  → Data retention policy (7 years for KYC records per PMLA)
```

